      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subjects offered in the term '2014FA': LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- Chemistry department: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- subject title from the library: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- number of enrolled students in the library subject: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- responsible faculty name from the TIP subject: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME\n- offer department name from the TIP subject: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the TIP subject's responsible faculty MIT ID: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID\n- minimum number of enrolled students in the library subject within window: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- total number of Chemistry subjects offered in '2014FA': TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- department name: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- academic year description: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\n- maximum enrollment for IAP activities: IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.MAX_ENROLLMENT\n- IAP activities: IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.MAX_ENROLLMENT\n- Mathematics department: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- advance sign-up required: IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.ENROLLMENT_TYPE\n- not cancelled: IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.IS_CANCELLED\n\n## Join Keys\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n\n## Question\nFor subjects offered in the term '2014FA' by the Chemistry department, show the subject title from the library, the number of enrolled students in the library subject, the responsible faculty name from the TIP subject, the offer department name from the TIP subject, the minimum number of enrolled students in the library subject within a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the TIP subject's responsible faculty MIT ID, and also include the total number of Chemistry subjects offered in '2014FA'. Additionally, for each academic year, show the department name, the academic year description, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the maximum enrollment for IAP activities offered in that year by the Mathematics department (considering only activities that require advance sign-up and are not cancelled), and for each department, include a grand total for all activities in the format of (department name, null, total variance and stddev). Present all these columns in the following order: subject title, number of enrolled students, responsible faculty name, offer department name, windowed minimum number of enrolled students, total Chemistry subjects in '2014FA', department name, academic year description, total variance, and total standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP). Do not return any rounded answers."
